  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-03-23T21:54:57.705Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hello, This has been on my mind for months on this idea.\nEver since we swapped to the way we go about counting what's on the model for the actual rank, the ranks became almost meaningless, specially if the said person had a generic animation on that is not even rendered(particle animations also count as 2 materials).....\nSo, i want to suggest a hybrid system.\nOriginally, everything was counted that was not visible.\nand the current one counts everything.\nSo, ingame you will noticed when you click on users and check their stats, you have \nOriginal, and below that\nPrefer/filtered, i want to change the filtered to Hidden/animations.\n\n-------------------------------\nExample:\nSo, Say i have a model that is 1 skin mesh, and 3 materials.\nBut i have a sword, pear, and a bear on it for animations\nIt will still show in original the true stats, while underneath it.\nfor animations/hidden, it will show 1 skin mesh, 3 meshes, 5-6 materials.\nDoing this, we can tell who is actually optimizing their models.\nAnd who is not.\n\nSo, We can see what is going on for said model more(more detailed).\nAnyways, what are your thoughts?\n~Todd",
